t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054394 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12919" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054394 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $2(3 x-1) +2$ for $x=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054394 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51bb6ac7-5c24-5805-85ba-9c697f4360b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054394 #edb/ref 1074 "We replace $x$ with $-3$ in the expression and evaluate the parentheses first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3x-1)+2 & = \\\\ 2(3\\cdot (-3)-1)+2 & = \\\\ 2(-9-1)+2 & = \\\\ 2(-10)+2 & = \\\\ -20+2 & = \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054395 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054395 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $x - \\dfrac{3}{2}y$ when $x=2$ and $y=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054395 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "caf5354e-e240-5515-94c7-6c3caa2063af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054395 #edb/ref 1074 "Replacing $x$ with $2$ and $y$ with $-2$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{3}{2}y & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-2) & = \\\\ 2+(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-2) & = \\\\ 2+3 & = \\\\ 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054424 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13069" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054424 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $2-\\dfrac{u}{4}$ for $u=\\dfrac43.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054424 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6acd4bf9-8cf9-5a35-a1f5-a9a01766af87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054424 #edb/ref 1074 "Replacing $u$ with $\\dfrac43$ in the expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{u}{4} & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{1}{4}u & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{4}{12} & = \\\\ 2-\\frac{1}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{6-1}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054838 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054838 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054838 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054838 #edb/ref 10